(3183376, 444937, 23141, '<td valign="top">Midtones are a little bit too dark here.  Also?  If this was a set-up shot?  That hat looks too small for her head and the dress seems out of place with your more simplistic fence and glowing orange lighting.  I''d try plain white, or anything without a pattern.  That being said, this is a cute portrait for the album.  Wonder how it would look in black and white.</td>', 'Midtones are a little bit too dark here.  Also?  If this was a set-up shot?  That hat looks too small for her head and the dress seems out of place with your more simplistic fence and glowing orange lighting.  I''d try plain white, or anything without a pattern.  That being said, this is a cute portrait for the album.  Wonder how it would look in black and white.', '2007-01-04 23:30:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3183377, 444557, 61413, '<td valign="top">Nice bold use of colour - in both the foreground and background.</td>', 'Nice bold use of colour - in both the foreground and background.', '2007-01-04 23:30:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(3183382, 446047, 47316, '<td valign="top">Really cool. Nice choice on the black and white. It would be better I think if the shadow of the fence was as dark as the top of the mountains to balance the photo out a bit.</td>', 'Really cool. Nice choice on the black and white. It would be better I think if the shadow of the fence was as dark as the top of the mountains to balance the photo out a bit.', '2007-01-04 23:31:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(3183388, 444620, 47316, '<td valign="top">I love the softness of this, it''s a nice change because a lot of people chose a very sharp and sometimes harsh renderings of their images. The thing that bothers me is so much of the foreground is out of focus that it''s really distracting</td>', 'I love the softness of this, it''s a nice change because a lot of people chose a very sharp and sometimes harsh renderings of their images. The thing that bothers me is so much of the foreground is out of focus that it''s really distracting', '2007-01-04 23:33:25.000000', NULL, 1),
