(3215085, 446461, 53572, '<td valign="top">ooo, lovely lovely lovely.<br/> <br/>my only niggle is the little lines in the vignetting, where the tone isn''t as smooth as it could be.  i''ve found one way to get rid of that is to do a very slight noise treatment to the gradient layer.  that shouldn''t affect the detail of the image, or appera overly noisy, but it helps to break up the lines between the tonal gradients.</td>', 'ooo, lovely lovely lovely. my only niggle is the little lines in the vignetting, where the tone isn''t as smooth as it could be.  i''ve found one way to get rid of that is to do a very slight noise treatment to the gradient layer.  that shouldn''t affect the detail of the image, or appera overly noisy, but it helps to break up the lines between the tonal gradients.', '2007-01-11 22:43:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3215962, 446053, 53316, '<td valign="top">Heh, great concept and nice out of the box shot.  Great technically although I find the light around the crotch region a little bit strange.</td>', 'Heh, great concept and nice out of the box shot.  Great technically although I find the light around the crotch region a little bit strange.', '2007-01-12 00:57:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3216133, 446504, 67841, '<td valign="top">Everyone seems to offer suggestions for post, so I''ll throw one in for pre -- knowing how hot that sky was going to be, I would have put a few more shots in the bag in case I couldn''t salvage the sky later.  <br/> <br/>In this scenario I can picture a shot where you got much closer to the cows, framing more cow heads in the shot and going a bit more profile, moooving your perspective down the line of the fence.  I would have raised my camera height a bit, too in order to crop more sky out of the shot.<br/> <br/>Some days you just can''t save a sky in post!  Well, you sorta can...  When the ''Best of 2006'' challenge is complete, take a look at my entry to see what I did to save a blown sky that took up 50-60% of my image!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Everyone seems to offer suggestions for post, so I''ll throw one in for pre -- knowing how hot that sky was going to be, I would have put a few more shots in the bag in case I couldn''t salvage the sky later.   In this scenario I can picture a shot where you got much closer to the cows, framing more cow heads in the shot and going a bit more profile, moooving your perspective down the line of the fence.  I would have raised my camera height a bit, too in order to crop more sky out of the shot. Some days you just can''t save a sky in post!  Well, you sorta can...  When the ''Best of 2006'' challenge is complete, take a look at my entry to see what I did to save a blown sky that took up 50-60% of my image! ', '2007-01-12 01:23:40.000000', NULL, 0),
